# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  pc2-node Environment Variables (template)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values you want enabled.
# .env is gitignored and survives `git reset --hard origin/main` during
# update.sh, so put per-node secrets HERE rather than in ecosystem.config.cjs.
#
# All variables are OPTIONAL — pc2-node runs with sane defaults if none are set.
#
# Loaded automatically at boot via `dotenv/config` (see pc2-node/src/index.ts).
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Server / runtime
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Port the Express HTTP API + WebSocket listens on. Default: 4200 (set in
# ecosystem.config.cjs). Override here for local dev or multi-instance.
# PORT=4200


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  IPFS Cluster pinning (v1.2.7+)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# DEFAULT: ENABLED. Every community pc2-node auto-replicates pins to the
# Elacity supernode mesh (Contabo + InterServer + eventually GCloud) on
# fresh install with ZERO operator action. The default URL + shared
# community token are baked into pc2-node/src/services/clusterPin.ts.
#
# Abuse protection: per-IP rate limiting at the supernode (30 req/min +
# burst 20) gives bounded exposure even though the token is public.
# Per-node rotatable tokens are slated for v1.2.8.
#
# OVERRIDE (use a different cluster — e.g. self-hosted): set both vars.
# Cluster Pinning Services API endpoint (HTTPS):
# SUPERNODE_CLUSTER_PIN_URL=https://your-cluster.example.com/pin

# Bearer token (operator-issued by your own cluster admin):
# SUPERNODE_CLUSTER_PIN_TOKEN=<your-token-here>

# DISABLE entirely (opt out of cluster pinning, only use local Helia + DHT):
# SUPERNODE_CLUSTER_PIN_URL=
# SUPERNODE_CLUSTER_PIN_TOKEN=

# Replication policy (how many cluster peers should hold each pin).
# Defaults: min=2, max=2 (one redundant copy across the cluster).
# Raise to 3/3 once GCloud joins for full 3-peer replication.
# SUPERNODE_CLUSTER_PIN_REPLICATION_MIN=2
# SUPERNODE_CLUSTER_PIN_REPLICATION_MAX=2

# TLS handling — certificates are always verified. Supernode IPs are
# checked against their `*.ela.city` certificate (utils/tlsTrust.ts).
# Do not set NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0.


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Legacy supernode forwards (still supported alongside cluster)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Single-supernode pin forward (pre-cluster mechanism). Still active in
# v1.2.7+ — fires in parallel with cluster forward if configured.
# Historically pointed at gcloud `ipfs.ela.city`.
# ELACITY_PIN_FORWARD_URL=https://ipfs.ela.city

# Multi-supernode REST API fan-out (comma-separated).
# SUPERNODE_PIN_MIRRORS=https://node1.example.com,https://node2.example.com

# Supernode RPC pool (Web3 reads — Particle Auth, marketplace, indexer).
# Comma-separated list of authoritative Base RPC URLs (Alchemy / Infura /
# self-hosted reth). Prepended to the public fallback chain at boot.
#
# ⚠ STRONGLY RECOMMENDED for any node whose users will mint on Elacity Market.
# Without this, Particle Auth's getPrimaryAssets() burst (~15-25 RPC calls
# during the mint flow) can rate-limit all 5 default public providers
# simultaneously, causing "RPC endpoint returned too many errors" in the
# wallet and the Particle sign dialog never appearing.
#
# Get a free Alchemy key (300M CU/month, ~25-30 req/s):
#   1. Sign up at https://alchemy.com (free, 5 min)
#   2. Create app → Base Mainnet → copy the HTTPS endpoint URL
#   3. Paste below
#   4. cd ~/pc2.net && pm2 reload ecosystem.config.cjs --only pc2 --update-env
#   5. Confirm in pm2 logs: [rpc] RPC pool initialized with 6 endpoints (1 supernode first)
#
# Will become unnecessary in v1.2.8 when the supernode RPC proxy at
# https://rpc.ela.city/base is baked into pc2-node/src/static.ts as the default.
#
# SUPERNODE_RPC_URLS=https://base-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/YOUR-KEY-HERE


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  IPFS bootstrap / network
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Override the default Elacity supernode bootstrap multiaddrs.
# Leave unset to use the hardcoded production list in src/storage/ipfs.ts.
# ELACITY_IPFS_MULTIADDRS=/ip4/x.x.x.x/tcp/4101/p2p/<peer-id>


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  AI providers (opt-in — pc2-node auto-detects which are configured)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Anthropic Claude (https://console.anthropic.com/)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# OpenAI (https://platform.openai.com/api-keys)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Google Gemini (https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey)
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=...

# xAI Grok (https://console.x.ai/)
# XAI_API_KEY=xai-...

# Local Ollama (http://localhost:11434 if running on same host)
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Communication gateways (opt-in)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Telegram bot (https://t.me/BotFather → /newbot)
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=<bot-token>

# WhatsApp via Baileys uses a session file in pc2-node/data/whatsapp/.
# No env var; session is established by scanning a QR on first run.


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Lit Protocol / Chipotle (encryption + secure-view)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Defaults are baked into the codebase + root .env.example. Override here
# only for testing custom Lit Actions or alternative backends.

# LIT_ACTION_CID=bafkreihvm4zkyuefnuptlbdins6cmd2mbslj2xgnyzz3ssdg2ggg3jtkk4
# MEDIA_ACTION_CID=bafkreihw7brius3xw2u7ltjac26hoqudulkc6mfwqrjxtrobanz2ryhvsq
# LIT_BACKEND=chipotle


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Migration notes for existing operators
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# If you previously set SUPERNODE_CLUSTER_PIN_URL/_TOKEN directly inside
# `ecosystem.config.cjs` (e.g. on a Jetson canary), the next git pull will
# reset that file to the tracked version. update.sh's migration helper
# auto-copies inline ecosystem values to this .env file BEFORE the reset
# (added in v1.2.7), so existing custom tokens survive transparently.
#
# In v1.2.7+, leaving these vars unset gives you the default Elacity
# community cluster automatically. You only need to set them if you want
# to use a DIFFERENT cluster or DISABLE cluster pinning entirely.
